/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:178:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:179:Fill holes inside a large template frame using shape-matched outside sprites.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:180:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:181:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:182:- bg = most common color. One large monochrome frame object (template).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:183:- Inside the frame: holes of various shapes (non-frame-color regions).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:184:- Outside the frame: small monochrome sprites scattered on bg.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:185:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:186:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:187:- Crop to the frame's bounding box; fill entirely with frame color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:188:- For each hole, find an outside sprite whose shape matches (rotation/flip allowed).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:189:- Fill the hole with the matched sprite's color. If multiple sprites match, use the most frequent color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:190:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:191:Key insight: Sprites act as shape-coded color keys — their shape identifies which hole they fill, their color determines the fill color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:192:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:193:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:194:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:195:<reference_puzzle index="11" source="eval" puzzle_id="446ef5d2" lines="8-20">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:196:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:197:Assemble scattered rectangular pieces into a rectangle at an L-marker corner.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:198:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:199:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:200:- bg = most common color. Non-bg rectangular pieces scattered on the grid.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:201:- 3-pixel L-marker (2x2 minus one cell) tags the corner; the gap is the corner cell.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:202:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:203:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:204:- rect_col = most common color across all piece pixels; all outer rectangle edges must be rect_col.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:205:- Translate pieces (no rotation) to tile the rectangle; touching edges must match, with rect_col as wildcard.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:206:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:207:Key insight: rect_col acts as wildcard during edge matching — only non-rect_col pixels at shared boundaries must agree.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:208:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:209:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:210:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:211:<reference_puzzle index="12" source="eval" puzzle_id="bf45cf4b" lines="7-19">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:212:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:213:Scale up a monochrome control sprite by stamping a polychrome tile at each filled pixel.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:214:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:215:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:216:- bg = background color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:217:- Two foreground objects (8-connected): a monochrome rectangular sprite with bg holes (control), and a polychrome square tile (block).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:218:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:219:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:220:- For each cell in the control sprite's bbox: if filled, stamp a copy of the block tile; if bg, leave a tile-sized bg region.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:221:- Output grid dimensions are (control_h × tile_h) by (control_w × tile_w).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:222:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:223:Key insight: The control sprite acts as a binary mask that gets "pixel-scaled" by the tile — each pixel expands to a full tile copy or empty space.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:224:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:225:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:226:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:227:<reference_puzzle index="13" source="eval" puzzle_id="36a08778" lines="8-21">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:228:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:229:Simulate water falling from top-edge sources, pooling on shelves, and cascading off edges.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:230:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:231:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:232:- bg = most common color; water = rarest non-bg; shelf = other non-bg.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:233:- Sources: water clusters touching top row. Shelves: horizontal segments.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:234:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:235:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:236:- Water falls down from sources, painting bg cells as water.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:237:- On hitting a shelf, it spreads across the shelf span plus one cell past each end.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:238:- From those overflow positions, water resumes falling independently.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:239:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:240:Key insight: Each shelf splits a stream into two at its edges, creating a branching waterfall tree.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:241:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:242:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:243:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:244:<reference_puzzle index="14" source="eval" puzzle_id="3e6067c3" lines="7-20">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:245:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:246:Connect framed squares via colored bridges following a control-pixel sequence.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:247:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:248:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:249:- bg = background. Border color forms equal-sized framed squares with unique inner fill colors.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:250:- Control row below squares: colored pixels read left-to-right encode visitation order.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:251:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:252:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:253:- Start at the square matching first control color c0.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:254:- For each consecutive pair (ci, ci+1), find the ci+1-colored square aligned in the same row or column band, preferring nearest.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:255:- Draw a bridge colored ci between the pair, spanning the gap with inner-square thickness.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:256:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:257:Key insight: Row/column-band alignment plus proximity resolves ambiguity when inner colors repeat.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:258:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:259:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:260:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:261:<reference_puzzle index="15" source="eval" puzzle_id="80a900e0" lines="69-82">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:262:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:263:Extend diagonal rays outward from outer-border segments adjacent to diamond shapes on a checkerboard.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:264:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:265:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:266:- Checkerboard bg (two most common colors).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:267:- Hollow diamond outlines (8-pixel) in a non-bg color (inner border).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:268:- Short diagonal line segments in another non-bg color adjacent to each diamond edge (outer border).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:269:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:270:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:271:- For each outer-border segment, determine the outward direction (perpendicular to the segment, away from the diamond).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:272:- From each endpoint of the segment, cast a diagonal ray outward, painting over bg pixels with the segment's color until hitting a non-bg pixel or the grid edge.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:273:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:274:Key insight: Rays emit only from the two endpoints of each outer-border segment, not every pixel, and travel diagonally away from the diamond.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:275:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:276:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:277:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:278:<reference_puzzle index="16" source="eval" puzzle_id="0934a4d8" lines="75-90">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:279:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:280:Reveal the rectangular patch hidden by the solid marker using the grid's reflection symmetries.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:281:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:282:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:283:- A square colored pattern with one solid rectangular marker color occluding a patch.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:284:- The visible pattern has horizontal and vertical reflection symmetry on a large lower/right strip.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:285:- The top and left outer strips also expose transpose counterparts for cells not recoverable by those reflections.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:286:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:287:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:288:- Find the unique color whose full extent is a solid rectangle; this rectangle is the output region.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:289:- Infer the reflected strip start as the smallest row/column offset whose lower/right strips are mirror-consistent, ignoring marker pixels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:290:- For each marker pixel, copy the unique non-marker value in its horizontal/vertical reflection orbit; if that orbit is entirely hidden in the outer strip, use the transposed top/left-strip counterpart.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:291:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:292:Key insight:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:293:The marker is not part of the pattern; it covers a missing rectangle whose cells are still determined by the visible mirror or transpose copies elsewhere in the grid.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:294:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:295:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:296:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:297:<reference_puzzle index="17" source="eval" puzzle_id="9aaea919" lines="38-51">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:298:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:299:Transfer sprites from red-marked lanes to green-marked lanes, recoloring and stacking.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:300:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:301:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:302:- bg = most common color. Red (2) and green (3) thin bars define vertical lanes.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:303:- Each lane contains repeated identical monochrome sprites in an evenly spaced vertical grid.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:304:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:305:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:306:- Each red lane's sprites turn grey (5); their count transfers to the nearest green lane.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:307:- New sprites fill empty lattice slots bottom-up, using the source shape recolored to the destination lane's sprite color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:308:- All marker bars are removed.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:309:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:310:Key insight: Sprite count is conserved across lanes — red sprites become grey, and equally many new sprites stack into the green lane's regular grid.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:311:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:312:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:313:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:314:<reference_puzzle index="18" source="eval" puzzle_id="fc7cae8d" lines="9-21">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:315:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:316:Align a central rectangle to two colored frame-edge controls via rotation/reflection.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:317:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:318:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:319:- bg grid with two solid-colored border edges (distinct non-bg colors).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:320:- A central filled rectangle with 1px colored guide edges on two sides, colors matching the frame controls.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:321:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:322:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:323:- Rotate/mirror the object so its guide edges face the same sides as the matching frame controls.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:324:- Crop off the 1px guide edges from aligned sides.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:325:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:326:Key insight: Guide-edge colors encode target frame sides; the correct dihedral transform matches both simultaneously.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:327:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:328:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:329:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:330:<reference_puzzle index="19" source="eval" puzzle_id="247ef758" lines="35-46">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:331:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:332:Move colored sprites from the left strip into a framed area at marker-defined targets.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:333:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:334:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:335:- bg background; rectangular frame on right with colored markers on its edges; sprites in a narrow left strip separated by a constant-color divider column.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:336:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:337:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:338:- For each color, target rows/cols are where both opposite frame edges share that color. Targets are the Cartesian product.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:339:- Erase each sprite from the left and stamp it centered at every target. Higher sprites cover lower ones.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:340:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:341:Key insight: One sprite replicates to a grid of row × column marker intersections.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:342:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:343:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:344:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:345:<reference_puzzle index="20" source="eval" puzzle_id="135a2760" lines="6-19">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:346:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:347:Repair noisy periodic patterns inside frame-delimited grid regions.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:348:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:349:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:350:- Frame color (most common) forms full rows/cols, dividing the grid into rectangular regions.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:351:- bg (second most common) fills empty space; each region contains a small colored tile repeated periodically with a few corrupted pixels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:352:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:353:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:354:- For each region, find the bounding box of non-bg content.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:355:- Infer the smallest repeating tile that explains the pattern (majority vote per residue position), requiring it repeat at least 2x per axis.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:356:- Replace the region with the clean tiled version.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:357:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:358:Key insight: Tile dimensions are unknown and must be inferred; prefer the smallest tile with genuine repetition over one that memorizes the entire region.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:359:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:360:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:361:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:362:你的任务：
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:363:以参考题为标杆，运用发散性思维进行创新扩展。请发挥创造力，构思全新且巧妙的推理谜题。用中文创造全新的 ARC 谜题描述。
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:364:创新方式包括但不限于：
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1557639258/3/prompt.md:365:**机制重组**：将多道参考题各自的核心机制提取出来，组合成一个新的多步管道，用到新的场景。
